WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:12.812
After the art gallery, Mom wanted some answers.

2
00:00:12.813 --> 00:00:16.996
"What's going on in the attic?" she demanded.

3
00:00:16.997 --> 00:00:19.715
The children looked at each other.

4
00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:23.026
"What was that light?" asked Mom.

5
00:00:23.027 --> 00:00:25.177
"And that book?"

6
00:00:25.178 --> 00:00:29.123
"We found some old books and a photo album,"

7
00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:33.917
Mandy started to explain, but Vinnie glared at her.

8
00:00:33.918 --> 00:00:37.560
"Hmmm," said Mom, suspiciously.

9
00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:41.817
"Well, that attic does have to be cleaned out."

10
00:00:41.818 --> 00:00:43.226
"We can do it,"

11
00:00:43.227 --> 00:00:47.258
said Vinnie, hoping to change the subject.

12
00:00:47.259 --> 00:00:51.014
"Okay, put everything into boxes," said Mom.

13
00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:55.603
"Who knows? Something valuable might be up there."

14
00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:58.943
Mom went into the kitchen.

15
00:00:58.944 --> 00:01:03.750
"That was close!" Mandy sighed.

16
00:01:03.751 --> 00:01:09.309
"Why did you tell her about the album?" Vinnie asked, annoyed.

17
00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.824
"I wasn't going to lie," protested Mandy.

18
00:01:13.825 --> 00:01:15.456
Vinnie shrugged.

19
00:01:15.457 --> 00:01:19.014
"Well, let's start cleaning the attic."

20
00:01:19.015 --> 00:01:23.296
The children took some empty boxes upstairs.

21
00:01:23.297 --> 00:01:28.249
But the minute they got to the attic, they forgot about packing.

22
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:32.154
Vinnie picked up the album and opened it.

23
00:01:32.155 --> 00:01:38.672
"It's beautiful," gasped Mandy at the photo.

24
00:01:38.673 --> 00:01:42.207
The old man was sitting in a room.

25
00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:46.882
There was only a low table in the center of the floor.

26
00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:52.055
A vase of flowers was glowing on top of the table.

27
00:01:52.056 --> 00:01:55.887
"It looks like . . . ," said Mandy.

28
00:01:55.888 --> 00:02:04.092
Before she could finish her sentence, the children fell down the dark tunnel.

29
00:02:04.093 --> 00:02:07.715
They landed inside a box of some kind.

30
00:02:07.716 --> 00:02:12.751
Red silk curtains covered the openings on either side.

31
00:02:12.752 --> 00:02:16.424
Whatever they were in, it was moving.

32
00:02:16.425 --> 00:02:21.965
"Ouch!" Mandy slid and bumped against one side.

33
00:02:21.966 --> 00:02:24.730
Vinnie slammed into her.

34
00:02:24.731 --> 00:02:28.678
Then they both slid to the other side.

35
00:02:28.679 --> 00:02:34.790
Vinnie tried to stand up, but he banged his head against the low ceiling.

36
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:39.345
"We're trapped in a moving box," cried Vinnie.

37
00:02:39.346 --> 00:02:42.461
He poked his head between the silk curtains.

38
00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:45.969
"Whoa!" he gasped.

39
00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:51.185
Mandy looked too. "Wow!" she cried.

40
00:02:51.186 --> 00:02:54.660
"No wonder we're bouncing around!"

41
00:02:54.661 --> 00:02:59.640
The children were in a kind of little house on long poles.

42
00:02:59.641 --> 00:03:02.646
Two men were carrying them.

43
00:03:02.647 --> 00:03:08.437
Fancier and bigger houses on poles were behind and in front of them.

44
00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:12.903
Men with swords rode on horses everywhere.

45
00:03:12.904 --> 00:03:17.301
"We're in some kind of parade," cried Vinnie.

46
00:03:17.302 --> 00:03:20.088
"Look at that, Mandy!"

47
00:03:20.089 --> 00:03:23.167
Vinnie pointed to two horsemen.

48
00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:27.402
They carried a flag with a symbol of two birds on it.

49
00:03:27.403 --> 00:03:31.877
People in the street bowed their heads as they passed.

50
00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:37.252
Mandy ducked her head back inside and noticed their clothes.

51
00:03:37.253 --> 00:03:41.173
"Look at what we're wearing!" she cried.

52
00:03:41.174 --> 00:03:45.475
They wore robes with wide belts around their waists.

53
00:03:45.476 --> 00:03:48.539
"What's this backpack thing?"

54
00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.435
Vinnie pointed to some folded fabric on Mandy's back.

55
00:03:53.436 --> 00:03:54.976
"I don't know.

56
00:03:54.977 --> 00:04:00.164
But my legs feel crushed," complained Mandy.

57
00:04:00.165 --> 00:04:03.605
"I can't move them around."

58
00:04:03.606 --> 00:04:09.110
Mandy tried to kick her legs, but her skirt was too tight.

59
00:04:09.111 --> 00:04:14.168
"These look like Japanese kimono," said Vinnie.

60
00:04:14.169 --> 00:04:23.907
"That's it! We're in Japan!" she exclaimed excitedly.
